      "message": "`slugify` in `slug/core.py` now takes an optional `max_length` and never cuts a word in half. I added a test for it, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass.\n\n- **Truncation:** if the slug is longer than `max_length`, it is cut back to the last whole word that fits, with no trailing dash. For example, `slugify(\"hello big world\", max_length=12)` returns `\"hello-big\"`.\n- **No fit:** if even the first word is longer than `max_length`, it returns `\"\"` rather than cutting that word. You may prefer a different fallback for that case.\n- **Default:** with `max_length` left out, the output is unchanged.\n\nThe new test, `test_max_length_never_cuts_mid_word`, covers a limit that falls mid-word, one that falls exactly on a word end, one that fits only the first word, one too small for any word, and a limit longer than the slug.",
